# The Publisher Test moved to the standalone Publisher Blueprint app.
# The `!` force flag is required: tools/brand-content-readiness.html is
# intentionally kept in the publish directory as a fallback, and without
# the flag Netlify would serve that file instead of honoring the redirect.
# Listed before /uploads/* so old /uploads links resolve in a single hop.
#
# TO REVERT to the old on-site tool: delete the four rules below, then
# repoint the nav links in all 12 top-level pages + tools/ back to
# tools/brand-content-readiness.html and restore the sitemap.xml entry.
/uploads/brand-content-readiness        https://blueprint.jeffhallstead.com/  301!
/uploads/brand-content-readiness.html   https://blueprint.jeffhallstead.com/  301!
/tools/brand-content-readiness          https://blueprint.jeffhallstead.com/  301!
/tools/brand-content-readiness.html     https://blueprint.jeffhallstead.com/  301!

# The Founder's Ceiling Quiz and the SDG Alignment Advisor were sunset.
# Both files are deleted, so no `!` flag is needed here — nothing would be
# served from these paths anyway. Old links land on the case study that
# tells the story of each tool rather than a dead end.
# Must stay ahead of the /uploads/* catch-all below, which is matched in order.
/tools/founders-ceiling-quiz          /case-study-founders-ceiling-quiz  301
/tools/founders-ceiling-quiz.html     /case-study-founders-ceiling-quiz  301
/uploads/founders-ceiling-quiz        /case-study-founders-ceiling-quiz  301
/uploads/founders-ceiling-quiz.html   /case-study-founders-ceiling-quiz  301
/tools/sdg-alignment-advisor          /case-study-sdg-advisor            301
/tools/sdg-alignment-advisor.html     /case-study-sdg-advisor            301
/uploads/sdg-alignment-advisor        /case-study-sdg-advisor            301
/uploads/sdg-alignment-advisor.html   /case-study-sdg-advisor            301

/test  https://blueprint.jeffhallstead.com/  301

/uploads/*  /tools/:splat  301

# Legacy Ghost blog URLs (pre-2026 site) that Search Console still crawls.
# Only paths with a genuine equivalent page are redirected; the old topical
# articles have no counterpart and are left to 404 so Google drops them
# (redirecting them to the homepage would be flagged as soft 404s).
/how-i-work-with-new-clients/*        /content-studio   301
/how-i-work-with-new-clients          /content-studio   301
/case-study-sustainable-exchange      /case-study-sae   301
/conta                                /contact          301
/page/*                               /                 301
